teddy bridgewater was officially  introduced yesterday he'll be the  starter at least for 2020  and pj walker previously known as philip  walker signed away from the xfl  yesterday was the day that teams could  begin signing xfl players and the best  player in the xfl star for the houston  roughnecks who were 5-0 before the xfl  had to shut down due to the covet 19  situation he is reunited with matt rule  who was with pj walker at temple now  he'll be in a position to compete to be  the backup to teddy bridgewater he did  some great things in the xfl chris i  know you didn't watch it your loss pj  walker was very very good running and  throwing the ball and it was just a  matter of time before he landed in the  nfl multiple teams were looking at him  the seahawks had multiple scouts at his  last game and the panthers with that  connection to matt rule reel him in  yeah i get it and you know you're right  i didn't watch xfl i watched pj walker  though there was a number of times where  you know i caught him on tv saw the  highlights you know certainly heard  about what he was doing you know he was  impressive even when he was you know  with the colts you know and pre-season  football he's got a quick release he  throws perfect spirals he's very  accurate and i think a lot of people  thought this would happen that he would  end up back with matt rule makes a lot  of sense he's got a similar skill set to  teddy bridgewater so that'll make for a  nice quarterback room uh but good for  b.j walker as a guy you know we like to  see those success stories a guy that  takes advantage of an opportunity that's  given to him he took it he was the star  of that league you know and hopefully he  or at least he hopes he can revive his  career in the nfl and get a chance to  play there at some point  another guy who had a decent season with  the xfl jordan ta'amu he has been signed  by the kansas city chiefs he'll have a  chance to compete to be on the depth  chart behind patrick mahomes and with  the carolina panthers picking up pj  walker chris they were able to unload  one of their quarterbacks a guy who  ultimately played in 13 games last year  with 12 starts kyle allen he gets sent  to washington reunites with former  panthers coach ron rivera and the  panthers get a fifth round pick for  their trouble that's not bad  when you undrafted when you sign a guy  undrafted and kyle allen and you can  flip him for a fifth round pick a couple  of years later if your new coaching  staff decides he's not going to fit with  what they're trying to do  no doubt well you know and we're seeing  you know coaches feel warm and cozy with  the people they know  matt rule signs pj walker yeah ron  rivera knows kyle allen you know scott  turner the offensive coordinator  coordinator there in washington he wants  to implement a system you need to have a  quarterback in the room in the building  that understands the system and can go  out and run practice be a tutor to  dwayne haskins at this point you know  listen i don't think kyle allen's coming  in here to like challenge dwayne haskins  as the starting quarterback but if  things fell apart for dwayne haskins now  you have a guy to sit here and go hey we  trust kyle allen he knows the offense he  played a lot last year he had some great  moments he really did you know i don't  think he's a starting quarterback  caliber type talent but i think kyle  allen is one of the better backups of  football now and into the future here  for a few years so makes a lot of sense  for the washington redskins and their  coaching staff  it makes me wonder where alex smith fits  in in the equation he has said he wants  to play  ron rivera has said don't rule out alex  smith you know and it feels like ron  rivera is a little ambivalent about  dwayne haskins i just wonder how this is  all going to play out in the coming  weeks and months especially if there's  no off season program for ron rivera to  get an early look at how alex smith is  performing if he's able to get on the  field how dwayne haskins looks how hard  is he working you know chris and and we  haven't delved down this rabbit hole yet  this morning but the more i think about  where we currently are in society and i  think about these group gatherings and  the facilities shut down if there's an  offseason program  the players are going to be in the same  solution situation that a lot of people  are right now which is they are going to  be working at home they're going to be  participating in meetings from home  they're going to be working out on their  own at home it's going to require a hell  of a lot of discipline it's going to be  a real test for younger players who may  be still in the process of maturing to  embrace everything they need to do  without being in that group that applies  via peer pressure and just presents the  impetus to do what you need to do you're  going to have to you're going to have to  prove to be a self-starter on a  consistent basis to get to where you  need to be in this off season program  yeah no it's not going to be easy for  players coaches anybody man i mean poor  new head coaches in the nfl trying to  implement your system you know with  nobody in the building the young  quarterbacks of the league like you're  mentioning that's going to be really  difficult you know hey yeah you can  learn through video conference face time  whatever it may be you can do all your  workouts you can go over to the field  and throw footballs but can you get  useful like walk through reps you know  the actual getting in the moment i'm in  the shotgun and i'm seeing the blitz  come and i've got to get the experience  of the walkthrough and the practice and  all of that  yeah players are going to miss that and  it's going to hurt the young players  more than anybody so  it's not going to be easy you're going  to see how these teams are going to  adjust i don't know how they're going to  do it but we saw it a little bit not too  long ago in the strike here we saw good  old jimmy harbaugh right my favorite  coach in football not uh but he had a  successful san francisco 49er team right  on a strike here and that's when he went  in with jim schwartz and gave him the  aggressive handshake because jim  schwartz had told them it was going to  be tough to have a successful year  without an off season so uh if jim  harbaugh can do it i'm saying anybody  can do it well schwartz took it farther  than that he was telling me you have no  chance just no chance why even bother  basically but here's the thing and this  is where teams need to be thinking  creatively they need to fashion an  offseason program that does indeed  embrace the technologies that are  available to ensure that guys are  engaged in these meetings that they are  teaching them effectively through their  web connections that they are working  out at home and that they are  accountable because you've got hundreds  of thousands of dollars in workout  bonuses that are tied to this as well so  yeah right while we're in this weird  state of limbo and it's not like the nfl  is going to make any announcements  prematurely on anything they plan to do  every team should be coming up with a  way to implement the offseason program  with all of their players at home  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports

